-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld points see coefficients only through Fr²-invariants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, with $\pi$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism with $Fr\,x\equiv x^r \pmod \pi$. Let $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ be a homomorphism with $v\!\det g=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^n$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^\times$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $\Gamma\le G$ containing a $z$ with $\sigma z$ scalar and $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ and a $w$ with $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$, let $\Gamma'$ consist of the elements of $\Gamma$ with even $v\!\det\circ\sigma$, let $\rho$ be the projectivisation of $\sigma$, and assume the image of $\Gamma'$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ has finite vertex stabilisers and finitely many orbits on the vertices of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O,K_0)$. Let $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be proper and flat, and let $\Theta$ assign, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:Onr\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (a family of $B$-submodules of the base-changed full lattices with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions and homotheties and nondegenerate at every prime) to the $\mathcal O$-morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$; assume $\Theta$ is natural in $B$, invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action (if $\psi'=\psi\circ Fr^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, then the values agree), has, over algebraically closed fields with $\pi$ nilpotent and fixed $\psi$, surjective fibre map whose fibres are precisely the twisted $\Gamma$-orbits, and is universal among such natural twisted-invariant families. Then for every such $B$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, and any two $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi,\psi':Onr\to B$ agreeing on all $y$ with $Fr(Fr\,y)=y$, one has $\Theta(\psi,P)=\Theta(\psi',P)$.
--
--   This records that a Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation $\Theta$ of a proper flat $\mathcal O$-scheme depends on the coefficient homomorphism $Onr\to B$ only through its restriction to the $Fr^2$-fixed subring, the unramified quadratic subring of $Onr$; the twisted invariance alone gives this for $\psi'=\psi\circ Fr^{2k}$, and the statement extends it to all pairs of coefficient maps agreeing there. It is used in the analysis of the $\mathcal O$-points of such a quotient, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.specPoint_eq_specMap_comp_of_map_pt_eq_act_pt_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.specPoint_eq_specMap_comp_of_map_pt_eq_act_pt_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient).
